     The mmaacc__ffrroomm__tteexxtt() and mmaacc__ttoo__tteexxtt() functions return the value 0 if
     successful; otherwise the value -1 is returned and the global variable
     _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the error.

CCOOMMPPAATTIIBBIILLIITTYY
     POSIX.1e does not define a format for text representations of MAC labels.

     POSIX.1e requires that text strings allocated using mmaacc__ttoo__tteexxtt() be
     freed using mac_free(3); in the FreeBSD implementation, they must be
     freed using free(3), as mac_free(3) is used only to free memory used for
     type _m_a_c___t.

